# Copy to `.env` if you want to override any defaults before
# `docker compose up`. Every variable here is OPTIONAL — the FrameCAD
# team server boots a working single-team instance with no .env at all.
#
# The team server stores team identity, locks, and publish history in a
# local SQLite database. It does NOT store CAD files — those live in your
# team's Google Shared Drive (see ../docs/google-workspace-setup.md).

# ── OPTIONAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# TCP port the server listens on.
# PORT=42130

# Bind address. Default 0.0.0.0 (LAN-facing by design).
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# Trust X-Forwarded-For. Set to 1 ONLY when the server sits behind a trusted
# reverse proxy (nginx/Caddy) — it makes the per-IP enroll/login brute-force
# throttles bucket by the real client instead of the proxy's single IP. Leave
# unset for a directly-exposed LAN server (an untrusted client could otherwise
# spoof the header). Default: off.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Where SQLite + the setup-PIN file live. In Docker this is the mounted
# /data volume; for local dev it defaults to ./data next to the source.
# DATA_DIR=/data

# Pino log level (fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace).
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Optional Discord/Slack incoming-webhook URL. When set, each in-app problem
# report (the desktop's "Report" button) is also posted to this webhook so a
# mentor sees it in chat. Reports always show in the admin "Reports" page
# regardless. Works with a Discord or Slack webhook URL as-is.
# FRAMECAD_ISSUE_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/XXX/YYY
